---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About the P4A">
  <main>
    <div class="container pt-24">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <header class="mb-14">
          <h1 class="mb-3 text-5xl text-p4a-ink font-bold">About Playbook for America</h1>
          <p class="text-xl max-w-prose leading-relaxed tracking-wider">
            <!-- Playbook for America (P4A) is an independent, nonpartisan nonprofit operating a civic technology platform
            that transforms citizen-driven ideas into structured Playbooks designed for adoption, execution, and measurable public impact. -->
            Playbook for America (P4A) is an independent, nonpartisan nonprofit operating a civic technology platform that transforms citizen-driven ideas into structured Playbooks designed for adoption, execution, and measurable public impact, supported by AI-assisted research and refinement tools.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section class="mb-14">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-ink font-bold mb-2">Our Mission</h2>
          <p class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
            The P4A exists to improve how government works by giving people a meaningful voice in shaping democratic ideas and priorities in the United States.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Organized as a nonpartisan nonprofit, P4A operates an online platform where citizens and government officials can crowdsource, discuss, and rank ideas and programs, with a focus on
            <!-- refining the strongest ideas into structured, execution-ready proposals capable of delivering measurable public benefit. -->
            refining the strongest ideas into structured, scoped, and implementation-ready Playbooks designed to move from adoption to funded, activated programs with measurable public impact.
            Our aim is to elevate the strongest proposals from all corners of the nation and encourage more people to actively participate in developing solutions that lead to real-world impact and tangible public benefit.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-14">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-ink font-bold mb-2">Our Vision</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            We envision a United States where public policy is informed by the collective intelligence of its people, institutions are effective, trusted, and supported by strong civic infrastructure, and civic life is inclusive and healthy. In this future, citizens and public servants work together to move ideas from discussion to action—strengthening communities at home and helping the United States play a responsible role addressing global challenges to make the world a better place.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-14">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-ink font-bold mb-2">Our Values</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            P4A is grounded in a commitment to nonpartisanship, openness, and respect for diverse perspectives. We believe the best ideas can come from anywhere, that constructive dialogue is essential to a healthy democracy, and that transparency and fairness are critical to building trust. We value collaboration between citizens and government, and we are guided by a focus on practical, evidence-informed solutions.
          </p>
        </section>


        <section class="mb-14">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-ink font-bold mb-2">Our Approach</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Playbook for America is grounded in the belief that civic participation must be structured to be effective.
            Open dialogue is essential, but durable progress requires disciplined refinement, defined ownership, and clear implementation pathways.
            A Playbook is considered implementation-ready when it is clearly defined, responsibly scoped, and supported by defined ownership and planning pathways.
            Our approach combines broad civic input with structured review to produce proposals that institutions can responsibly implement.
            Each stage of the lifecycle includes structured assessment to ensure ideas are strengthened responsibly before advancing toward adoption and delivery.
          </p>
        </section>


        <section class="mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-3xl text-p4a-ink font-bold mb-2">Founders Backstory</h2>
          <p class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
            I'm <a class="underline text-p4a-ink hover:text-p4a-body-text" href="https://linkedin.com/in/jknapp" target="_blank">John Knapp</a>,
            I build software that helps people improve their lives and communities and help organizations execute effectively so they can deliver more impactful results.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
            I believe most Americans want to improve government, strengthen democracy, renew civic life, and help the United States contribute to a better world.
            The way I see it, far fewer feel invited or equipped to act on those ideas—and when people don't see how their participation can lead to real progress, they disengage.
          <p class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
            I want P4A to engage and activate those citizens by moving good ideas through a disciplined lifecycle that turns public input into real-world implementation.
            I believe in the potential to drive collaboration between citizens and government to increase alignment, accelerate implementation, and strengthen public impact.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Let's build the next 250 years of American civic life.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
